1
00:01:34,285 --> 00:01:40,285
How to Train Your Dragon: Homecoming is a animation,
fantasy, adventure film directed by Tim Johnson.

2
00:03:08,571 --> 00:03:14,571
It's been ten years since the dragons moved to the Hidden World, and even though Toothless doesn't live in
New Berk anymore, Hiccup continues the holiday traditions he once shared with his best friend.

3
00:04:42,857 --> 00:04:48,857
But the Vikings of New Berk were beginning to forget
about their friendship with dragons.

4
00:06:17,142 --> 00:06:23,142
Hiccup, Astrid, and Gobber know just what to do to keep
the dragons in the villagers' hearts.

5
00:07:51,428 --> 00:07:57,428
And across the sea, the dragons have a plan of their own...

6
00:09:25,714 --> 00:09:31,714
Hiccup (voice), played by Jay Baruchel.

7
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:06,000
Astrid (voice), played by America Ferrera.

8
00:12:34,285 --> 00:12:40,285
Gobber (voice), played by Craig Ferguson.

9
00:14:08,571 --> 00:14:14,571
Zephyr (voice), played by Madalyn Gonzalez.

10
00:15:42,857 --> 00:15:48,857
Fishlegs (voice), played by Christopher Mintz-Plasse.

11
00:17:17,142 --> 00:17:23,142
Nuffink (voice), played by Liam Ferguson.

12
00:18:51,428 --> 00:18:57,428
How to Train Your Dragon: Homecoming is a 2019 animated short
film by DreamWorks and directed by Tim Johnson.

13
00:20:25,714 --> 00:20:31,714
Set before the epilogue of How to Train Your Dragon: The Hidden World (2019), it was
simultaneously released  on DVD and aired on NBC on December 3, 2019.
